{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I need to share my findings from the technology review. Personal phones cannot be used for school recordings. The project must use district tablets instead. Source files must be stored in the restricted OralHistory drive, and all recordings must be deleted exactly 45 days after the final class presentation. Storing source files in that restricted drive does not prohibit publishing consented recordings on the public school website. Additionally, the technology plan must include a secure-storage configuration record documenting this setup."}
